WEBVTT

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.310
Thank you.

00:01:35.308 --> 00:01:36.968
Bandits, we must be near that stronghold.

00:01:37.356 --> 00:01:38.956
Maybe that's where they're holding Shiller a prisoner.

00:01:40.204 --> 00:01:41.164
Your friends!

00:01:42.476 --> 00:01:43.956
We're walking right into our trap.

00:01:44.876 --> 00:01:45.636
For the last time.

00:01:45.996 --> 00:01:48.176
Are you going to tell us the secret of your gyro compass or not?

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:51.576
You're wasting your time, Captain.

00:01:52.236 --> 00:01:54.636
Go back and tell your mysterious leader, whoever he is.

00:01:54.892 --> 00:01:56.432
That this invention belongs to the Marines.

00:02:12.508 --> 00:02:13.828
Come back and tell the Capitan.

00:02:14.524 --> 00:02:15.624
There are only a few Americans.

00:02:16.796 --> 00:02:17.856
We can take care of them.

00:02:40.876 --> 00:02:42.176
Only a handful of soldiers.

00:02:42.516 --> 00:02:44.456
Ah, that will make it more simple.

00:02:45.324 --> 00:02:47.964
We will have no difficulty in capturing them.

00:02:48.332 --> 00:02:49.572
They're fighting the Marines, mister.

00:02:50.124 --> 00:02:52.384
And before it's over, your bandits will know they've been in a battle.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.720
off from here as long as the ammunition lasts. We have to make every shot count.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.630
Pat, did you ever see swamp grass growing in the riffle?

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:37.380
No.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:42.510
You got him.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:50.940
So why?

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:51.960
We should have joined the Navy.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.670
A couple of those hand grenades.

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:55.410
What are you going to do?

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.970
I'm going to find their ammunition supply and toss in a pineapple.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:03:58.670
You'll never make it.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:03:59.650
We're outnumbered 100 to one.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.560
We've taken that chance. We've got to save Schiller.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.600
Okay, we'll keep them busy, and when we hear the explosion, we'll start moving in.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.710
Don't take any wooden nickels, Colton.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:06.740
She's got to make. She won't last long.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:00.820
Rato! Rato!

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.190
Take it easy, old man. I'll have you out of here in a jiffy.

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:42.720
Good old USA again.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.900
Yeah, and the first thing I'm going to do is get me a great big T-bone steak,

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:52.520
smothered in mushrooms and fried onions with huckleberry pie and ice cream.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:54.840
There you go, Mac. Always thinking of your stomach.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:58.080
Good news, fellas. They just got a radio message from headquarters.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:07:59.960
Saying they're going to give my gyro couples a...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:22.710
final pass when we get back to the base. Great! I hope it works. Don't forget to wash your

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:27.300
neck, soldier. Never mind the wisecracks. I got a date with the swellest gal in town.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:29.650
What's the matter with her?

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:35.000
blind or something? No, just smart. She knows class when she sees it. And she's driving

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:46.440
out in her own car to pick me up. That's what gals think of me. Must be the hair tonic

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:54.500
that gets them. Hair tonic my eye. It's my personality, my friend. Personality. Is she

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:59.840
a good dancer? Good dancer? It's like walking on air when you step out with her. Well.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:00.920
So long, heartbreaker.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:04.900
Hope you don't have to walk home.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:23.290
You're a lifesaver, Frances.

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:27.660
Just have time to go to the flying field and see your brother Land.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:29.960
But promise, Mac, I...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.800
Who, McGowan?

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:32.730
He won't be out for an hour.

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:33.810
He's having foot trouble.

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:34.870
Foot trouble?

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:35.330
Yeah.

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:51.730
Where's the plane now?

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:29.790
Congratulations, Sergeant.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.120
Sergeant. Your gyro compass will certainly revolutionize flying. Thank you, sir. I'm

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:38.860
going to Colonel Bennett and tell him that with your invention, nothing can stop us from

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:53.940
landing at Halfway Island. Sir? Thomas A. Edison, Jr. Great. So is the invention. Captain

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:57.300
Grayson is going to recommend me for that flight to Halfway Island. You mean to tell me that

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.880
that contraption actually flies the plane? Not exactly.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.210
but it keeps the plane from veering off its course.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:05.590
Oh, I hate to have you starting off on another trip so soon.

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:08.360
Remember, sis, I'm in the Marines.

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:09.920
Don't cry, Francis.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:11.600
I'll be your big brother while he's away.

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:14.300
I'll big brother you if you don't tell me where you hid my shoe.

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:15.200
Your shoe?

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:17.200
You mean you can't find it?

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:18.700
Don't act innocent or royal.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:20.600
How's McGowan?

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:22.500
You're familiar with dress regulations?

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:23.600
Yes, sir, but...

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:24.240
No, BOTS.

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:25.680
Go back to your quarters and finish dressing.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:34.820
I have to check in at the hangar.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:38.090
Now, that's a pal for you.

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:40.260
Accusing me of stealing his shoe.

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.360
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.720
Well, all's fair in love and war.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:53.410
It steered a true course, in spite of all our efforts to throw it off.

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:57.010
Gentlemen, this invention of Sergeant Chilis seems to be the solution of our problem.

00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:58.740
How does it strike you, Douglas?

00:11:59.490 --> 00:11:59.970
Alarm's sorry.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.460
Sorry, Colonel, but I still wish you'd give up this hopeless attempt to establish a landing field on Halfway Island.

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:11.870
I don't think that instrument can combat the magnetic dead spot that has caused the destruction of every ship and plane that's tried to reach the island.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:16.320
Of course, your feelings are naturally influenced by the fact that you were forced to give up a similar project.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:20.810
And you'll give it up, too, after you've sacrificed the lives of the men you're sending on this flight?

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:28.160
I appreciate your sincerity, Douglas, but unfortunately, every step in the progress of civilization is fraught with danger and difficulty.

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:29.960
The government needs a landing field.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.140
and halfway island, we're determined to go through this project at any cost.

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:53.590
I shall expect a radio report hour by hour on the progress of your trip.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:54.190
Yes, sir.

00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:55.430
Well, good luck, men.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:57.110
And a happy landing.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:57.710
Thank you, sir.

00:12:58.490 --> 00:12:59.070
Thank you.

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:08.590
There they are.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:10.540
I'd like to say goodbye to my sister, sir.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:11.780
All right, Sergeant.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:12.560
I'll meet you at the plane.

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:16.820
Goodbye, sir.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:19.540
I hate to leave you with these two leather necks.

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:20.360
Don't worry, Bill.

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:21.340
She'll be in good hands.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:22.160
Thanks, Mike.

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.120
That's the first nice thing you've ever said about me.

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:26.580
All right, then.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:27.040
Let's go.

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:28.180
Well, goodbye.

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:29.900
Goodbye.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.140
Let these two mugs kill each other.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:32.440
So long.

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:34.490
Don't forget to bring back a souvenir.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:16.000
that plan down on halfway island, those men will. I hope so. Just to show Douglas the Marines

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:19.550
always finish what they start. Strange that he should be so opposed to our building a

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:23.980
landing field on that island. You don't think that he... That's easy to understand. Douglas

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:27.950
has been trying to build a floating airport near that island for some time. When we complete

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:29.960
our project, his undertaking will be...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.490
He stands to lose a fortune.

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:48.140
Any messages, Miss Martin?

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:49.120
No, Mr. Douglas.

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:50.780
I've got some important work to do.

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:53.000
I don't want to be disturbed.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:53.920
Very well, sir.

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:12.240
Yes. Yes. Call you back later.

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:20.150
Yes, sir.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:22.410
That last haul, we've got over $300,000 worth of loot stored up in this cave.

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:28.180
As far as I'm concerned, I'll take my share right now and give this island back to the natives.

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:29.900
You'll take your share?

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.720
when the tiger shark gets ready to give it to you

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:32.660
and not before.

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:33.800
Tiger shark.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:34.740
Tiger shark.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:36.860
Every day we risk our lives for him.

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:38.390
We don't even know who he is.

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:39.210
C.C., who is he?

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:40.870
You'd better be careful what you say.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.380
Better men than you have tried to find out

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:44.520
who the tiger shark really is

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:45.840
and you know what happened to them.

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:49.960
Tiger shark.

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:05.000
We are 3-0 receiving.

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:16.900
Advise the Tiger Sharks that everything will be in readiness to receive them.

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:18.970
M7-0 signing off.

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:37.920
Men, here's one we can't afford to miss.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:39.420
And it isn't loot this time.

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:41.070
It's our necks.

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:42.860
I'll say it's our necks.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.760
If we ever get those Marines after us...

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:45.820
Oh, there's nothing to worry about.

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:47.830
We'll crack them up as fast as they send them over.

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:55.520
One-nine standing.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.520
Come away, Schiller. Stay with us.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.110
We're pulling for you, Leatherneck.

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:10.400
They're certainly making a remarkable time.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:13.100
Yes, but they haven't hit the dead spot area yet.

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:15.170
The speed they're making will be heading into it soon.

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:22.330
Pedro, you stand by the sound detector and call us the moment you pick up that motor.

00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:23.280
Please, sir.

00:19:02.650 --> 00:19:04.110
Repair the magnetic ray guard.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.870
She is halfway up.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:44.360
Location, 4320.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:45.760
Location, 4320.

00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:47.360
Attitude, 2,000 feet.

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:48.940
Attitude, 2,000 feet.

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:50.390
Border, northeast, 1.

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:51.990
Border, northeast, 1.

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:52.570
Border!

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:02.040
Look, let it get up there.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:04.570
Must be edging into that dead spot.

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:05.430
Give me those controls.

00:20:05.790 --> 00:20:16.090
Of course, there's a purchasing report.

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:39.190
Good work, men. Off contract.

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:43.890
Gibson, you and I, Ben, go down there and clean up that wreckage.

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:47.980
Order out every available plane.

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:48.420
Yes, sir.

00:20:48.690 --> 00:20:50.930
Are you, Henderson, ready over the base at Honolulu's top? Search immediately.

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:51.510
Yes, sir.

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:53.100
Get me near your headquarters at once.

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:53.600
Mr. Douglas isn't in.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:54.960
Well, I miss Shelley.

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:57.210
Mr. Douglas wanted to see me about something.

00:21:57.410 --> 00:21:59.450
Oh, yes, but he was called out suddenly.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:05.180
be back any moment. Won't you please wait? Well... You better stay. Must be something

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:09.220
important. You're sure you won't mind? Of course not. I have to get back to barracks

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:15.680
right away. I'll see you later. Goodbye. Goodbye. And thanks a lot. Won't you sit down? Thank

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:15.920
you.

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:09.530
Colonel Bennett's office, please. Colonel Bennett is not here.

00:23:10.030 --> 00:23:15.110
When Colonel Bennett returns, please tell him that Miss Schiller is bringing her brother's gyro compass to headquarters.

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:16.260
I'll tell him.

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:22.120
Colonel, I can't understand your attitude of this matter.

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:25.840
Sir, Miss Schiller just telephoned. She'd find her brother's compass.

00:23:26.330 --> 00:23:27.970
Coming through the barracks with it right away.

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:29.580
Miss Schiller's brother? You sure?

00:23:30.670 --> 00:23:31.490
Where'd she telephone from?

00:23:31.650 --> 00:23:32.510
She now say, sir.

00:23:32.940 --> 00:23:33.520
You hear that, Douglas?

00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:35.380
Sergeant Shiller's compass.

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:37.460
Yes, it sounds incredible.

00:23:38.210 --> 00:23:40.170
If this is true, it may clear up the entire mystery.

00:23:40.910 --> 00:23:42.230
I wish you'd let me know if it's so.

00:23:43.120 --> 00:23:43.700
Well, I...

00:23:44.850 --> 00:23:46.250
I think I'd better go back to my office.

00:24:21.120 --> 00:24:21.820
from the Tiger Shark.

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:22.830
Frances Schiller

00:24:22.830 --> 00:24:23.370
is on her way

00:24:23.370 --> 00:24:24.030
to the Marine Base

00:24:24.030 --> 00:24:24.830
with that gyro compass.

00:24:25.240 --> 00:24:25.680
It's up to you

00:24:25.680 --> 00:24:26.060
to stop her

00:24:26.060 --> 00:24:26.720
before she reaches

00:24:26.720 --> 00:24:27.160
Colonel Bennett.

00:24:27.430 --> 00:24:27.810
Okay.

00:24:30.540 --> 00:24:46.840
I thought these old crates were condemned.

00:24:47.260 --> 00:24:47.460
Yeah.

00:24:47.830 --> 00:24:49.810
They're using a brand of aircraft target practice.

00:24:50.010 --> 00:24:50.210
Yeah?

00:24:50.430 --> 00:24:51.710
Where's the radio control crew?

00:24:51.910 --> 00:24:53.350
They're on the range, near the gun crew.

00:24:54.040 --> 00:24:55.160
Hey, wait till I make a contact, will you?

00:24:55.370 --> 00:24:55.650
Sure.

00:24:59.490 --> 00:24:59.970
I'll take a...

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.350
Wait, sir. Start the plane.

00:25:01.590 --> 00:25:02.030
All right, sir.

00:25:22.570 --> 00:25:23.940
Men's firing. Men's firing.

00:25:32.880 --> 00:25:34.740
Boy, we're sure going to town today.

00:25:35.150 --> 00:25:37.050
That's the third bullseye we've made in a row.

00:25:37.740 --> 00:25:38.900
Where do you get that we stuff?

00:25:39.460 --> 00:25:41.500
All you do is hook up a couple of little wires.

00:25:43.810 --> 00:25:45.170
Say, where did Douglas send for Francis?

00:25:45.970 --> 00:25:47.250
I don't know yet, sharpshooter,

00:25:47.750 --> 00:25:50.590
but when I talk to the lady, we may give you the details.

00:25:52.260 --> 00:25:53.980
Say, what do you mean, we?

00:26:15.960 --> 00:26:16.280
package.

00:27:03.930 --> 00:27:11.670
Contact complete, sir.

00:27:11.930 --> 00:27:12.590
Start the plane.

00:27:12.810 --> 00:27:13.230
Aye, sir.

00:27:57.520 --> 00:27:59.600
2-400, section 3-5.

00:28:00.092 --> 00:28:02.552
Range 2400, deflection 35.

00:28:03.324 --> 00:28:04.784
Commence firing. Commence firing.
